// pfodWeb NOTE: dedicated-hardware pin-exclusion audit, 2026-07-12.
// Board: uPesy ESP32-C3 Basic (a.k.a. "uPesy ESP32-C3 Low Power Basic" in
// uPesy's own docs/product listing - same board, USB_PRODUCT string in this
// variant's pins_arduino.h reads "uPesy ESP32C3 Basic"), ESP32-C3-MINI-1
// module on a narrow 2x-per-side breadboard-friendly carrier. This board's
// own pins_arduino.h declares TX=21, RX=20, SDA=3, SCL=10, SS=7, MOSI=6,
// MISO=5, SCK=4, A0-A5=0-5 (generic ESP32-C3 template aliases), and
// VBAT_SENSE=0 (aliased to BAT_VOLT_PIN). No board.json override existed
// before this audit (used the chip-level esp32c3/board.json default).
// Flagged by the discovery sweep for having VBAT_SENSE=0 declared but never
// individually reviewed. Sibling board uPesy_esp32c3_mini (near-identical
// pins_arduino.h) is being audited separately this wave - NOT assumed
// identical; verified independently below.
//
// Sources consulted:
//  - https://www.upesy.com/blogs/tutorials/upesy-esp32c3-basic-low-power-board-documentation-version-latest
//    Official uPesy documentation page for this exact board. States (French):
//    "La broche GPIO0 (non exposee) est utilisee par la carte pour mesurer
//    la tension d'alimentation" (GPIO0, not exposed, is used by the board to
//    measure the supply voltage) - vendor-confirmed dedicated battery-sense
//    pin, not broken out to a header pad despite the Arduino core's generic
//    A0=0 naming alias. Gives the measurement formula:
//    "V_BAT = 2 x (V_IO0_bits / 4095) x 3.3V" and provides example code
//    reading analogRead(0) - confirms a 2x multiplier (equal-ratio resistive
//    divider, i.e. R_series == R_shunt) ahead of the ADC, and explicitly
//    warns the reading is only valid when the board is battery-powered (USB
//    power present gives an incorrect result - out of scope for a static
//    capability audit, noted for the user).
//  - https://www.upesy.com/products/esp32c3-low-power-basic-board
//    Official product page, confirms "GPIO0 (not exposed) is used by the
//    board to measure the power supply voltage" and lists GPIO2/GPIO8 as
//    the strapping pins with pull-ups for BOOT mode - matches this chip's
//    existing pinNotes (2, 8, 9) already inherited from the esp32c3 chip
//    default, no change needed there.
//
// GPIO0 (VBAT_SENSE / BAT_VOLT_PIN / A0): confirmed onboard dedicated
// battery-voltage-sense pin via uPesy's own official documentation and
// product page (both independently state GPIO0 is not exposed on a header
// and is reserved for supply-voltage measurement), with a vendor-given 2x
// multiplier equivalent to a 1:1 (equal-value) resistive divider, giving an
// effective corrected reference of 3.3V * (R_series+R_shunt)/R_shunt =
// 3.3V * 2 = 6.6V for the raw ADC-to-battery-volts conversion. Per this
// project's battery/voltage-monitor KEEP policy, this pin's capabilities
// are left unchanged from the chip-level default (analog_input retained,
// not excluded) - only a documentation "note" was added, matching the
// established pattern (see e.g. esp32c3/ttgo-t-oi-plus's GPIO2). adc.
// defaultRefVolts is NOT changed board-wide (still "3.3") because the
// divider is wired only to this one dedicated pin, not to the board's other
// analog-capable pins.
//
// Alias-conflict check (playbook step): checked this board's own
// pins_arduino.h for any SDA/SCL/SS/MOSI/MISO/SCK/TX/RX alias landing on
// GPIO0: SDA=3, SCL=10, SS=7, MOSI=6, MISO=5, SCK=4, TX=21, RX=20 - none is
// 0, so no bus-capability contamination risk and no alias line needed
// deletion. No other declaration in this file aliases GPIO0 besides A0,
// VBAT_SENSE and BAT_VOLT_PIN.
//
// No LED_BUILTIN, BUT_BUILTIN, or any other button/LED alias is declared
// anywhere in this board's pins_arduino.h, and neither the uPesy
// documentation page nor the product page mentions an onboard user button
// or status LED for this specific board - section 7a (opportunistic
// button/LED check) found nothing to tag.
//
// See boardsDetails/esp32/esp32c3/uPesy_esp32c3_basic/notes.txt for the
// full research trail.

{
  "boardName": "ESP32C3",
  "displayName": "ESP32-C3 Dev Module",
  "family": "esp32",
  "pwm": { "min": 0, "max": 255, "method": "analogWrite" },
  "dac": {},
  "adc": { "bits": 12, "max": 4095, "defaultRefVolts": "3.3" },
  "inputOnlyGpios": [],
  "connections": ["serial", "ble", "tcp", "http"],
  "pinNotes": {
    "2": "Must be HIGH for normal boot",
    "8": "Must be HIGH or floating on reboot",
    "9": "Must be HIGH for normal boot"
  },
  "chipGpios": {
    "0":  { "capabilities": ["analog_input", "digital_input", "digital_output", "pwm_output"], "note": "VBAT_SENSE / BAT_VOLT_PIN - onboard battery-voltage sense, not physically exposed on a header pad per vendor docs (1:1 divider; vendor formula applies a 2x multiplier to the raw ADC reading, equivalent to an effective 6.6V corrected reference). Only valid when battery-powered, not on USB power. See pfodWeb NOTE above." },
    "1":  { "capabilities": ["analog_input", "digital_input", "digital_output", "pwm_output"] },
    "2":  { "capabilities": ["analog_input", "digital_input", "digital_output", "pwm_output"] },
    "3":  { "capabilities": ["analog_input", "digital_input", "digital_output", "pwm_output"] },
    "4":  { "capabilities": ["analog_input", "digital_input", "digital_output", "pwm_output"] },
    "5":  { "capabilities": ["analog_input_serial", "digital_input", "digital_output", "pwm_output"] },
    "6":  { "capabilities": ["digital_input", "digital_output", "pwm_output"] },
    "7":  { "capabilities": ["digital_input", "digital_output", "pwm_output"] },
    "8":  { "capabilities": ["digital_input", "digital_output", "pwm_output"] },
    "9":  { "capabilities": ["digital_input", "digital_output", "pwm_output"] },
    "10": { "capabilities": ["digital_input", "digital_output", "pwm_output"] },
    "11": { "capabilities": ["digital_input", "digital_output", "pwm_output"] },
    "20": { "capabilities": ["digital_input", "digital_output", "pwm_output"] },
    "21": { "capabilities": ["digital_input", "digital_output", "pwm_output"] }
  }
}
